CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --enforce-contract foo --apply-loop-contracts _ --no-standard-checks --unwinding-assertions --unwind 5
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[foo.loop_assigns.\d+\] line 19 Check assigns clause inclusion for loop .*: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^\[foo.assigns.\d+\] .*: FAILURE$
unwinding assertion .*: FAILURE$
--
This test checks that a loop with a contract nested in a loop without a contract
is checked against the write set of the enclosing function: the inner loop may
assign `g`, but `foo` has no assigns clause permitting this, so the assigns
clause inclusion check of the inner loop must fail. Before the fix, the inclusion
check was performed against the write set of the outer loop, which is never
initialised because the outer loop is not instrumented.
